        "collapsible_tab_UWQ8gk": {
          "type": "collapsible-tab",
          "name": "Overview",
          "settings": {
            "collapsible_tab_heading": "Overview",
            "collapsible_tab_text": "<h3>4WD Power for the Terrain 2WD Can't Handle</h3><p>The <strong>Mowrator S1 21″ 4WD</strong> puts power to all four wheels, giving you control on slopes, soft ground, and uneven terrain that a two-wheel-drive mower struggles with. Rated for slopes up to <strong>75% grade (37°)</strong>, it handles the demanding sections of your property while you stay in control from a comfortable distance with the included remote.</p><h4>Which battery should you get?</h4><p><strong>12Ah — $3,499:</strong> up to 1.5 hours of runtime and 0.75 acres per charge. The right call for smaller to mid-size lots where you'll finish well within one charge.</p><p><strong>18Ah — $3,999:</strong> up to 2.25 hours of runtime and 1.125 acres per charge. The right call for larger properties or when you'd rather not stop mid-mow to recharge.</p><p>Both share the same 21″ deck, adjustable cutting height, and 4WD platform — the battery is the only decision to make.</p><p><strong>One platform. Two runtimes. You pick the one that matches your yard.</strong></p>"
          }
        },
        "collapsible_tab_Uf69Wz": {
          "type": "collapsible-tab",
          "name": "Product Information",
          "settings": {
            "collapsible_tab_heading": "Product Information",
            "collapsible_tab_text": "<h2>Which Battery Is Right for You?</h2><p>The S1 4WD ships with either a 12Ah or 18Ah battery — same mower, same 4WD platform, different runtime.</p><p><strong>12Ah — $3,499</strong><br/>Up to 1.5 hours of runtime and coverage of up to 0.75 acres per charge. Best suited for smaller to mid-size residential properties.</p><p><strong>18Ah — $3,999</strong><br/>Up to 2.25 hours of runtime and coverage of up to 1.125 acres per charge. Ideal for larger properties or longer mowing sessions.</p><p>Both batteries use a 56V LiFePO4 platform.</p><h2>Cutting Power</h2><p>The 21″ steel cutting deck offers adjustable cutting height from <strong>1.5″ to 4.3″</strong>, with mulch, rear bag, or side discharge options depending on the job.</p><h2>Drive & Handling</h2><p>The 4WD drivetrain distributes power across all four wheels, giving the S1 traction on slopes up to <strong>75% grade (37°)</strong> — well beyond what a 2WD configuration can handle.</p><p>The S1 is operated via handheld remote control rather than autonomous navigation, so you stay in command of every pass.</p><h2>Warranty</h2><p>2 year warranty covering the main machine, remote, and battery — on both the 12Ah and 18Ah configurations.</p>"
          }
        },
        "collapsible_tab_X7L37G": {
          "type": "collapsible-tab",
          "name": "Warranty & Support",
          "settings": {
            "collapsible_tab_heading": "Warranty & Support",
            "collapsible_tab_text": "<p>Every Mowrator S1 4WD is backed by Mowrator's standard 2 year warranty, covering the main machine, the remote control, and the battery, on both the 12Ah and 18Ah configurations.</p><p><strong>What's covered</strong><br/><br/>Manufacturing defects and functional failures under normal residential use. Warranty service is handled through Mowrator's authorized repair network; you'll need proof of purchase (order date, model, and serial number) to file a claim.</p><p><strong>30 Day Money-Back Guarantee</strong><br/><br/>If the S1 4WD doesn't work out for your yard, return it within 30 days of delivery for a refund. Keep the original packaging on hand for the return window — it makes the process faster.</p><p><strong>Reporting an issue</strong><br/><br/>Inspect your mower on delivery. Shipping damage should be reported within 24 hours, and any other concerns within 7 days, to keep your claim eligible.</p><p><strong>Our role</strong><br/><br/>As your dealer, we're your first point of contact. Reach out to us for setup help, order questions, or to get a warranty claim started, and we'll coordinate directly with Mowrator on your behalf so you're not left navigating it alone.</p>"
          }
        },
        "collapsible_tab_HjeTwa": {
          "type": "collapsible-tab",
          "name": "Setup & Installation",
          "settings": {
            "collapsible_tab_heading": "Setup & Installation",
            "collapsible_tab_text": "<p>Getting the S1 4WD running takes about 15 to 20 minutes, most of it charging.</p><p><strong>In the box</strong><br/><br/>Mower body with 21 inch standard blade, battery (12Ah or 18Ah depending on your selection), 600W charger, wheels, grass outlet cover, Professional Remote Controller, tool bag, manual grass bag, mulching insert, and data cable.</p><p><strong>1. Charge the battery</strong><br/><br/>Before first use, fully charge the battery using the included charger. Connect the charger to a standard outlet and seat the battery securely in the charging port.</p><p><strong>2. Assemble the grass bag</strong><br/><br/>Check the bag for damage before installing. Slide the fabric onto the metal frame, then fasten the rubber strips around the bag opening to the frame.</p><p><strong>3. Choose your clipping mode</strong><br/><br/>For mulching, open the grass outlet cover and insert the mulching insert in the direction of the arrow. For bagging, attach the assembled grass bag. For discharge, no attachment is needed.</p><p><strong>4. Seat the battery</strong><br/><br/>Unlock the battery buckle, insert the battery into its compartment until secure, and close the buckle.</p><p><strong>5. Pair the remote</strong><br/><br/>Power on the mower. The remote connects to it wirelessly. Indicator lights on the mower confirm connection status: red means not connected, amber means connecting, green means ready to mow.</p><p><strong>6. Set your cutting height</strong><br/><br/>Adjust the deck to your starting height within the 1.5 to 4.3 inch range using the integrated height adjuster. Start higher on the first cut if your lawn hasn't been mowed recently.</p><p><strong>7. Clear the area and do a test pass</strong><br/><br/>Walk the yard first and remove sticks, toys, hoses, or debris. Keep people and pets clear of the mowing area. Run a short test pass in an open section before mowing the full yard.</p>"
          }
        },
        "collapsible_tab_czbJiW": {
          "type": "collapsible-tab",
          "name": "Specifications",
          "settings": {
            "collapsible_tab_heading": "Specifications",
            "collapsible_tab_text": "<p>Model: Mowrator S1 21″ 4WD<br/><br/>Drive: Four wheel drive, 4WD<br/><br/>Cutting width: 21 in<br/><br/>Cutting height range: 1.5 to 4.3 in, adjustable<br/><br/>Max slope rating: 75% grade (37°)<br/><br/>Battery: 56V LiFePO4, available in 12Ah or 18Ah<br/><br/>Runtime: up to 1.5 hours (12Ah) or up to 2.25 hours (18Ah)<br/><br/>Coverage per charge: up to 0.75 acre (12Ah) or up to 1.125 acres (18Ah)<br/><br/>Clipping system: mulch, rear bag, or side discharge<br/><br/>Control method: handheld remote control<br/><br/>Warranty: 2 years on main machine, remote control, and battery<br/><br/></p>"
          }
        },
