          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is this mower autonomous, like a robot mower?",
            "answer": "<p>No. It's a remote-controlled mower, not a self-navigating robot. You operate it with a handheld controller from wherever you're standing. It doesn't map your yard, use GPS, or run scheduled mows on its own.<br/><br/></p>",
            "icon": "none"
          }
        },
        "question_69jhiF": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What's the real difference between the 12Ah and 18Ah battery?",
            "answer": "<p>Runtime and coverage per charge. The 12Ah gives you up to 1.5 hours and covers up to 0.75 acres. The 18Ah gives you up to 2.25 hours and covers up to 1.125 acres. Both use the same 56V LiFePO4 battery platform and the same S1 4WD mower — only the battery capacity changes. If your lot is under half an acre, the 12Ah is plenty. Larger lots benefit from the 18Ah simply because you'll finish in one charge instead of stopping to recharge.<br/><br/></p>",
            "icon": "none"
          }
        },
        "question_8KCdGW": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How steep a slope can the 4WD handle?",
            "answer": "<p>Up to 75% grade (37°). If your yard has steeper sections, the Wide Wheels or Grip Tread Tire editions are rated for steeper terrain. Always mow across a slope rather than straight up or down it.<br/><br/></p>",
            "icon": "none"
          }
        },
        "question_EcA6Mx": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can it handle wet or overgrown grass?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes, within reason. The front-to-rear airflow system and lift blade are built to handle wet, matted grass without clogging. Very thick or heavily overgrown lawns may need a first pass at a higher cutting height before a second pass at your target height.<br/><br/></p>",
            "icon": "none"
          }
        },
        "question_BQYmLz": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I upgrade the battery later?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. Mowrator sells the 12Ah and 18Ah batteries separately, so if you start with the 12Ah and later want more runtime, you can add an 18Ah battery without replacing the mower.<br/><br/></p>",
            "icon": "none"
          }
        },
        "question_JjXiyk": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Who can operate it?",
            "answer": "<p>The remote is designed to be simple enough for most adults to pick up quickly. That said, it's still a machine with a spinning blade — keep children, pets, and bystanders clear of the mowing area while it's running.<br/><br/></p>",
            "icon": "none"
          }
        },
        "question_JxkamV": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Does it require regular maintenance?",
            "answer": "<p>Basic upkeep applies, similar to any mower: keep the blade clean and sharp, check for debris in the deck and airflow channels after use, and store the battery partially charged if it'll sit unused for a while.<br/><br/></p>",
            "icon": "none"
          }
        }
      },
